# RD-pareto sweep — post buttloop d>=2.0 cur_pow tuning fix
# 2026-05-14

## Change under test

In `forks/butteraugli_loop.rs`, `refine_aq_field_gpu_with_strategy_search_persistent`
now uses **distance-aware** `cur_pow` and `max_increase` defaults:

| target_distance | cur_pow | max_increase | Source |
|---|---|---|---|
| < 2.0 (LOW)     | 0.5     | 1.3          | GPU-tuned (Feb 2026, this corpus at d=1.0) |
| >= 2.0 (HIGH)   | 0.2     | 100.0 (≈no cap) | libjxl default (`enc_adaptive_quantization.cc:1106`) |

Pre-fix used `cur_pow=0.5, max_increase=1.3` for ALL distances. The
GPU-tuned values were calibrated at d=1.0 on a 3-image corpus; they
over-reclaimed good blocks at low quality (d>=2.0), costing 11pp on the
d=3.0 RD-pareto axis.

## How to reproduce

```bash
cargo run --release -p jxl-encoder-gpu \
    --features 'cuda encoder butteraugli-loop' \
    --example rd_pareto_vs_cjxl -- \
    --image .../02809272...png \
    --image .../0369d229...png \
    --image .../07b9f93f...png \
    --image .../a365e6541...png \
    --image .../terminal.png \
    --distance 0.25 --distance 0.5 --distance 1.0 \
    --distance 2.0 --distance 3.0 --distance 5.0 \
    --encoder gpu_e7 --encoder gpu_e8 --encoder gpu_e9 \
    --encoder cjxl_e7 --encoder cjxl_e8 \
    --out benchmarks/rd_pareto_post_buttloop_d3_fix_2026-05-14.tsv \
    --runs 1
python3 jxl-encoder-gpu/examples/analyze_rd_pareto.py \
    benchmarks/rd_pareto_post_buttloop_d3_fix_2026-05-14.tsv
```

## Sweep methodology

`benchmarks/rd_pareto_buttloop_sweep_2026-05-14.tsv` captured per-image
ratios for 15 alternate `(cur_pow, max_increase)` configurations at
d=3.0 on the 4 photo images. The libjxl default (`cur_pow_high=0.2,
max_increase_high=∞`) won at 97.0% mean ratio, beating baseline 108.0%
by 11pp. See `benchmarks/rd_pareto_buttloop_sweep_2026-05-14.tsv` for
all 15 configurations.

The sweep harness `examples/sweep_buttloop_tuning.rs` is retained so
future per-distance tuning can re-run quickly.

## Verification

| Distance | gpu_e8 PRE | gpu_e8 POST | Δ photos | Verdict |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| d=0.25 | 99.6% | 99.6% | +0.0pp | byte-identical (LOW unchanged) |
| d=0.50 | 99.6% | 99.6% | -0.0pp | byte-identical |
| d=1.00 | 103.7% | 103.3% | -0.5pp | byte-identical at d=1.0 |
| d=2.00 | 97.4% | 93.9% | **-3.6pp** | wins on 3/4 images |
| d=3.00 | 108.0% | **97.0%** | **-10.9pp** | wins on 3/4 images |

Photos = 4 CLIC images (excludes `terminal` screenshot; that has a
separate, structural 145-407% encoding gap consistent across all
distances — unrelated to the buttloop tuning). gpu_e9 == gpu_e8 across
all distances (early-exit gate fires).

corpus_regression test (33 cases, smart turnkey path) PASSES — the
smart pipeline uses `refine_aq_field_gpu_with_encode` which has its
own (simpler) tuning and is unaffected by this change.
